B2 G | (G2 A) | B2 d | {e}(d2 B) | c2 {c}B | (A2 G) | A2 {G}^F | G3 |]
w: nos Lais-saz_ nos Bal-lar_ en-tre nos,_ en-tre nos.
W:In English: At the coming of the bright season, eya, to begin the joy again, eya, and to annoy the jealous, eya, the queen wants to show that she is so full of love. Away, away, jealous ones, let us, let us dance among ourselves.
W:
W:II. El' a fait per tot mandar, - Eya,
W:Non sia jusqu'a la mar, - Eya,
W:Piucela ni bachalar, - Eya,
W:Que tuit non venguan dançar
W:En la dansa joioza. (Refrain)
W:(She has sent word everywhere, as far as the sea, that every girl and young man should come and dance in the joyful dance.)
W:
W:III. Lo reis i ven d'autra part, - Eya,
W:Per la dansa destorbar, - Eya,
W:Que el es en crematar, - Eya,
W:Que on no li voill' emblar
W:La regin' aurilloza. (Refrain)
W:(The king comes from elsewhere to break up the dance, for he is afraid someone will steal his April queen.)
